  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Major cities across India experienced a significant deterioration in air quality following the Deepavali festival, with New Delhi reporting levels in the 'severe' category. Air pollution measurements in parts of the capital reportedly exceeded World Health Organization guidelines by over 50 times. While residents in cities like Chennai, Mumbai, and Hyderabad also faced hazardous smog levels, the situation in New Delhi triggered an intensified political conflict. The Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) has alleged that the regional government engaged in a conspiracy, while the Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) and the Congress party have raised questions regarding the validity and potential manipulation of reported air quality index data. Authorities had previously attempted to tighten air pollution controls in the region, yet widespread use of firecrackers continued, contributing to the current environmental conditions affecting millions of residents across the country.",
